[h1]LiveWire - Electrical Skill Overhaul[/h1]

[b]Build 42.21+ · Singleplayer & Multiplayer[/b]

The power is out for good, but the lights do not have to be. Build your own off-grid electricity: solar panels, wind turbines and water wheels feed an inverter that powers the house around it, with batteries for the night.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/art/extended_banner.png[/img]

[h2]One subscription, three mods[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]LiveWire[/b] (required): generate, store and distribute your own power. Part 1.
[*][b]LiveWire Extended[/b] (optional, [b]new in 2.0[/b]): power whole buildings through breaker boards, room by room. Part 2.
[*][b]LiveWire - Viewpoint models[/b] (optional): 3D models, only if you use Project Viewpoint.
[/list]
Extended and the models need LiveWire, enabled before them.

[hr][/hr]
[h1]1. LiveWire, the base mod[/h1]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/diagram_en.png[/img]

[h2]How it works[/h2]

Solar 100 W, wind 400 W, water wheel 120 W. An inverter powers appliances within 20 tiles and ±3 floors, up to 1,500 W, with no cable per appliance. Surplus goes into power banks. Every device has an Electrical level, and your level makes the installation better.
While the public grid works, an inverter inside a building also draws up to a fifth of its power from the mains (sandbox option GridCharging, on by default).
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-01-getting-started]Getting started[/url]

[h2]Equipment[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/equipment_en.png[/img]

Placing needs a screwdriver, no level. Linking: solar panels and inverters level 3; wind turbines, water wheels and power banks level 2. Optional: breaker, battery alarm, soundproofing, vanilla backup generator, management computer.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-02-equipment]Equipment guide[/url]

[h2]Production[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/production_en.png[/img]

Solar output depends on direction: south 100%, east and west 85%, north 55%. Clouds, snow and dirt reduce it; rain cleans the panels. Wind produces from 10 km/h, at full power from 30 to 85 km/h. The water wheel works day and night.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-04-production-and-calculations]Production and calculations[/url]

[h2]Wiring & coupling[/h2]

Right-click a device, then LiveWire, then Connect to an inverter. A cable costs 1 wire per 4 tiles, range 12. Need more than 1,500 W? Couple a second inverter (Couple to an inverter, 1 Inverter Coupling Kit): a network holds 4 inverters, 6,000 W.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-03-wiring]Wiring guide[/url]

[h2]Inverter screen & management software[/h2]

The inverter screen switches lighting, equipment and main levers, and shows the watts of each circuit. LiveWire Monitor adds consumers, cable views, a three-day forecast and the last 30 events on a powered management computer.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-05-inverter-screen-and-software]Inverter screen and software[/url]

[h2]Water pump[/h2]

A water pump (Electrical 3) feeds plumbed fixtures within 15 tiles, from up to 8 adjacent rain collectors or [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3436537035]Useful Barrels[/url].
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-07-water-pump]Water pump guide[/url]

[h2]Recipes[/h2]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/recipe_book_en.png[/img]

16 crafting recipes, shown above, and 15 dismantling recipes (screwdriver): everything you craft can be dismantled except the solar cell. Pick up a device, even broken, then dismantle it from the crafting menu.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-08-recipes]Recipes[/url]

[h2]Electrical skill & safety[/h2]

Test batteries at Electrical 1, 3 and 5 for more detail. Live work has a shock risk, on by default: 50% at level 0, 0% at level 6+. Switch off the master inverter first; opening a breaker does not isolate it.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-10-electrical-skill-and-maintenance]Electrical skill and maintenance[/url]

[h2]Multiplayer[/h2]

The server checks every action; circuit choices and appliance states are saved and synchronised. Close both circuits before disabling the mod.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-12-multiplayer]Multiplayer guide[/url]

[hr][/hr]
[h1]2. LiveWire Extended, the optional add-on[/h1]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/diagram_extended_en.png[/img]

Carries the inverter's power to whole buildings and outdoor zones. Main jobs need Electrical 3.

[list]
[*][url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-14-livewire-extended#connect-a-whole-building]Connect a whole building[/url]: every floor and the basement. Optional strip around it: sandbox option Outdoor strip around a building (0 by default).
[*][url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-14-livewire-extended#power-terminal-and-zone]Outdoor power terminal[/url]: powers a drawn zone of up to 16 x 16 squares.
[*][url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-14-livewire-extended#breaker-boards]Breaker boards[/url]: 15, 20 or 30 A breakers, one per circuit. Some map houses have one prewired.
[*][url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-14-livewire-extended#twilight-switch]Breaker Twilight Switch[/url]: fitted on a breaker, it keeps that circuit on from dusk to dawn.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/equipment_extended_en.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/main/docs/images/diagrams/recipe_book_extended_en.png[/img]

[h2]Enable and remove[/h2]

Enable it in the mod list, after LiveWire. Not compatible with LG Extended Electricity or Knox Power. To remove it safely, an admin first switches every breaker back on from a board's menu.
[url=https://github.com/cyberbobjr/LiveWire/wiki/EN-14-livewire-extended]Full guide[/url]

[hr][/hr]
[h1]3. Viewpoint models[/h1]

[url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3809306528]Project Viewpoint[/url] users: enable LiveWire - Viewpoint models for 3D models of every device, Extended included.

[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

Works with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3725497089]Computer Mod[/url] and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798992436]Laptop Mod[/url] (optional). Original creation, not meant to run with other power-system mods. Licence MIT.

